    {
      "id": "62bf8b1d-eb74-4f9c-8df6-48df6ff40981",
      "name": "Template description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1136,
        2544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1152,
        "content": "# Track competitor ads and prices with Apify and Google Sheets\n\n## Who's it for\n\nE-commerce and retail teams that want to watch what rival brands advertise on Meta and what prices they charge, without a manual weekly research routine.\n\n## How it works\n\n- Trigger the workflow manually to launch a competitor sweep.\n- Search Facebook pages in your category and location with the Facebook Search Scraper Actor.\n- Pull active ads from each competitor page with the Facebook Ads Library Scraper Actor.\n- Extract the product URLs advertised in each ad card.\n- Scrape product name, description, price, and currency with the E-commerce Scraping Tool Actor.\n- Append or update each product row in a Google Sheet, matched by product ID.\n\n## How to set up\n\n1. Import the workflow JSON into n8n.\n2. Add your Apify API token as an Apify credential from Apify Console, Settings, Integrations.\n3. Connect a Google Sheets OAuth credential.\n4. Open the Facebook Search Scraper node and edit `categories`, `locations`, and `resultsLimit` in the body.\n5. Create a Google Sheet with columns `Product name`, `ID`, `Description`, `Price`, and `Currency`, then paste its URL into the Append or update row in sheet node.\n6. Run the workflow and confirm rows appear.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- An Apify account with an API token. Apify is the largest marketplace of tools for AI. 61,000 Actors to automate your business.\n- A Google account with Google Sheets access.\n\n## How to customize the workflow\n\nSwap the manual trigger for a Schedule Trigger to run a daily or weekly sweep, or change the category and location filters to cover a different market. You can also route results to Slack or Airtable if that fits your reporting stack."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
